# The ledger of `http/suffixes`: the Public Suffix List, which no standard
# library of the three holds. Go's `net/http/cookiejar` takes one through an
# interface and `golang.org/x/net/publicsuffix`, outside the standard library,
# answers it; Python and Rust have none. The list is publicsuffix.org's,
# version 2026-11-17_06-40-19_UTC, fetched 2026-11-18 into the scratch folder
# and made data by a one-off program; every expected value of the tests is
# the list's own test file's (tests/test_psl.txt, fetched 2026-11-18, public
# domain), 77 cases.

capability psl/suffix  the public suffix of a domain name, and whether ICANN's section says it
  heroes  suffixes.suffix_of, suffixes.Suffix
  go      net/http/cookiejar.PublicSuffixList.PublicSuffix
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    the list's algorithm: an exception prevails, else the longest rule, a wildcard's label taken for any, else the implicit `*`; `icann` says the prevailing rule's section, false for the implicit rule, as x/net/publicsuffix reports it. A name is read in ASCII, a label in another script as its A-label, as the rules are held; an address and a name with an empty label are refused `invalid`, where the list's test file answers null

capability psl/registrable  the registrable domain of a host: its public suffix and one label more
  heroes  suffixes.registrable_domain_of
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    `not_found` where the host is a public suffix itself; all 77 cases of the list's test file answered as it writes them, its names in other scripts given as A-labels

capability psl/is-suffix  whether a name is a public suffix itself, as a cookie's `Domain` is asked
  heroes  suffixes.is_public_suffix
  go      net/http/cookiejar.PublicSuffixList
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    a value of `(function(str) -> bool)` for `http.Session`'s `is_public_suffix`, which `http.store_cookies_by` asks

capability psl/version  which list the rules are made from
  heroes  suffixes.VERSION
  go      net/http/cookiejar.PublicSuffixList.String
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    the list's own VERSION line. The rules are the Mozilla Foundation's, under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, which the data module says

capability psl/update  the list read again at run time from a newer copy
  heroes  refused: the rules are data compiled in, as x/net/publicsuffix compiles its; a newer list is a newer release of Rebel, made by the same one-off program
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
